initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,\\text{d}s$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  | $0$ |  |  |  |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308692 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cc8319e7-c74a-546c-ac46-138a893fec53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308692 #edb/ref 1074 "Given the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} & t{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5t}\\end{bmatrix}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-1)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{5(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{5(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5s} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{5(t-1)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{\\int }_{1}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{5t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308723 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308723 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335081" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308723 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308723 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+y(t)+1 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ |  |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308723 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "47fdaa8b-a137-5a55-9e2b-f6799e375b7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308723 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}$ and $g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x(0) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & t{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} & (t-s){e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-(t-s)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-(t-s)} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1-{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308813 #edb/ref 1080 "applying a change of variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308813 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308813 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08a0e04b-fdf3-54cb-b350-9898e7a963ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308885 #edb/ref 1080 "evaluating at $t=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308885 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308885 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1323f90a-02bd-56b9-8366-20c0593acd49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308923 #edb/ref 1080 "\\text{L2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308923 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308923 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "16a95f78-5388-52c8-81fd-1590793a0892" #edb/ref 1759218